WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.731 --> 00:00:01.731 line:15%
[Jeff Goldblum] Hmm.

2
00:00:03.255 --> 00:00:04.088
Hmm.

3
00:00:04.088 --> 00:00:05.185
(laughter and applause)

4
00:00:05.185 --> 00:00:09.128
Hello there, I'm so glad you could join me today.

5
00:00:09.128 --> 00:00:11.089 line:15%
I'm Leonard Meshbesher--

6
00:00:11.089 --> 00:00:11.922 line:15%
(laughter)

7
00:00:11.922 --> 00:00:14.941 line:15%
The psychotherapist to the superheroes.

8
00:00:14.941 --> 00:00:16.470
They call me renowned.

9
00:00:16.470 --> 00:00:19.473
In any case, take a look at some of these sessions,

10
00:00:19.473 --> 00:00:22.712
and you'll see the kind of work that goes on here.

11
00:00:22.712 --> 00:00:25.373
So, I'm sensing some tension

12
00:00:25.373 --> 00:00:28.123
between the two of you right now.

13
00:00:29.035 --> 00:00:30.960 line:15%
Yes, I'm right?

14
00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:33.703 line:15%
[Professor X] She's been very passive-aggressive with me.

15
00:00:33.703 --> 00:00:34.715
You've got to be very frank and direct,

16
00:00:34.715 --> 00:00:36.552
can you do that, Storm?

17
00:00:36.552 --> 00:00:38.764
You know, we can't read your mind.

18
00:00:38.764 --> 00:00:42.931
Well, (chuckles) maybe he can.

19
00:00:43.388 --> 00:00:45.807
(electricity sizzles)

20
00:00:45.807 --> 00:00:47.359
Storm?

21
00:00:47.359 --> 00:00:49.416
Are you controlling my humidifier again?

22
00:00:49.416 --> 00:00:50.914
I don't want you to do that, Storm.

23
00:00:50.914 --> 00:00:52.331
Storm? Thank you.

24
00:00:54.446 --> 00:00:56.946
Superheroes help other people.

25
00:00:58.060 --> 00:00:59.779
That's what they're in the business to do.

26
00:00:59.779 --> 00:01:03.529
But so often, they've got issues around Dada.

27
00:01:04.837 --> 00:01:06.420
Daddy issues. Dada.

28
00:01:08.032 --> 00:01:10.793
How did it feel, is my question, Luke,

29
00:01:10.793 --> 00:01:14.960 line:15%
when you declared a boundary with your father.

30
00:01:15.358 --> 00:01:17.007
[Luke] He cut off my hand.

31
00:01:17.007 --> 00:01:20.251
I sure would like you to use those I feel statements.

32
00:01:20.251 --> 00:01:22.827
I feel bad, I feel sad, I feel--

33
00:01:22.827 --> 00:01:25.966
[Luke] I feel like flipping you off right now.

34
00:01:25.966 --> 00:01:27.175
Both of you.

35
00:01:27.175 --> 00:01:28.979
Okay, could have been more effective,

36
00:01:28.979 --> 00:01:31.805
I don't know why you didn't use the good hand.

37
00:01:31.805 --> 00:01:33.862
You could do a flip off much more effectively there.

38
00:01:33.862 --> 00:01:35.281
That reminds me of one of those

39
00:01:35.281 --> 00:01:36.114
hotel ding ding ding ding ding,

40
00:01:36.114 --> 00:01:37.793 line:15%
doesn't it, in the lobby?

41
00:01:37.793 --> 00:01:40.793 line:15%
You know what I judge your essential

42
00:01:42.265 --> 00:01:43.498
struggle to be?

43
00:01:43.498 --> 00:01:44.575
[Jon] What's that?

44
00:01:44.575 --> 00:01:46.270
I think it has something to do with your dad.

45
00:01:46.270 --> 00:01:48.945
If he were here right now in this room with us,

46
00:01:48.945 --> 00:01:50.780
what would you say to him?

47
00:01:50.780 --> 00:01:53.266
[Jon] I don't know.

48
00:01:53.266 --> 00:01:55.183
I'm not just a bastard.

49
00:01:56.941 --> 00:01:58.952
You're not just a bastard.

50
00:01:58.952 --> 00:02:01.485
I've got a surprise for you, Jon Snow.

51
00:02:01.485 --> 00:02:02.472
He's right here.

52
00:02:02.472 --> 00:02:03.642
Here's your dad, let's talk.

53
00:02:03.642 --> 00:02:05.505
(cheers and applause)

54
00:02:05.505 --> 00:02:09.255 line:15%
Trust that they will catch you, ready and ...

55
00:02:11.373 --> 00:02:12.439
And now Peter.

56
00:02:12.439 --> 00:02:15.106
And now just totally let go, go.

57
00:02:19.477 --> 00:02:20.894
[Spider-Man] Assholes.

58
00:02:22.683 --> 00:02:25.059
And what'd you learn from that?

59
00:02:25.059 --> 00:02:26.795
Life is unpredictable.

60
00:02:26.795 --> 00:02:30.137
When it comes to mental health, don't be a hero.

61
00:02:30.137 --> 00:02:31.054
You get it?

62
00:02:32.067 --> 00:02:34.250 line:15%
Call the Institute, and there you go.

63
00:02:34.250 --> 00:02:37.609 line:15%
There you go, right there, right there.

64
00:02:37.609 --> 00:02:40.359
Because, and one more final word,

65
00:02:42.886 --> 00:02:44.945
sometimes the greatest superpower--

66
00:02:44.945 --> 00:02:46.653
[Old Man] Hey!

67
00:02:46.653 --> 00:02:47.486
Dad?

68
00:02:47.486 --> 00:02:48.319
Who are you talking to?

69
00:02:48.319 --> 00:02:50.782
Dad, I've asked you (bleeps).

70
00:02:50.782 --> 00:02:53.510
I've asked when I'm working to not interrupt me.

71
00:02:53.510 --> 00:02:55.730
Can I ever have some (bleeps) privacy--

72
00:02:55.730 --> 00:02:58.541
All right, all right.
When I'm trying to work.

73
00:02:58.541 --> 00:03:02.708
Your mother wants you to know that dinner is ready.

74
00:03:03.029 --> 00:03:04.529
Oh, okay. Sorry.

75
00:03:07.429 --> 00:03:09.346
Ah, I know where I was.

76
00:03:12.387 --> 00:03:15.053
Sometimes the greatest superpower

77
00:03:15.053 --> 00:03:17.220
is being a great listener.

78
00:03:20.113 --> 00:03:23.446
(enthusiastic applause)

79
00:03:25.918 --> 00:03:27.933
That man is a genius.

80
00:03:27.933 --> 00:03:29.638
That man is a genius.

81
00:03:29.638 --> 00:03:31.138
I bow to that man.

